Year = {1977},
Volume = {27},
Number = {4},
Pages = {305-309},
Abstract = {Respiration in D. nasutum, an active protozoan predator, was
   investigated in relation to cell weight at 10, 15 and 20.degree. C by
   means of Cartesian diver microrespirometry. O2 uptake increased
   progressively over the 10-20.degree. C temperature range; a table of Q10
   related to weight is presented. Regression coefficients of log weight
   vs. log O2 uptake (b) were 0.96 at 10.degree. C, 0.98 at 15.degree. C
   and 1.00 at 20.degree. C. D. nasutum expended much higher levels of
   respiratory energy than a mainly sedentary carnivorous ciliate
